CORE
wrong.py

^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[assertion.1\] .* line 5 Python assertion: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
^\[.*\] .* Python assertion: SUCCESS$
--
The results of replace() are all those of CPython at once. (One assertion
per result needs one solver query each, as a failed assertion ends its
path, which takes minutes with refined strings.)
